## Task 2: Variadic Functions
Status: [DONE]

Spec: Section 4.2 — Last parameter may be variadic with `...` prefix.

```geoflow
fn sum(numbers: ...int) -> int {
    numbers.reduce(0, \acc, n -> acc + n)
}
sum(1, 2, 3)        -- 6
sum(1)               -- 1

fn printf(fmt: string, args: ...auto) { ... }
```

### What exists
- AST: `FunctionParameter.Variadic` bool field exists.
- Parser: `parseFunctionParameters` handles `...` before param name.
- Token: `ELLIPSIS` token type exists.

### What's missing
- Evaluator: `applyFunction` does not collect excess arguments into a List for
  the variadic parameter. When the last param is variadic, gather all remaining
  args into `&object.List{Elements: remainingArgs}` and bind it.
- Interaction with default parameters (variadic must be last).
- Tests: zero variadic args, multiple variadic args, variadic with preceding required params.

### Files to modify
- `internal/eval/eval.go` — `applyFunction`
- `internal/eval/eval_test.go` — new tests
- `examples/` — add example usage

### Completed: 2026-02-11
### Deviation: None — implementation matches spec.
- Modified `applyFunction`: variadic params excluded from `requiredParams` count.
- Modified `extendFunctionEnv`: when a param has `Variadic: true`, all remaining
  args are collected into `&object.List{Elements: remainingArgs}`. Zero variadic
  args produce an empty list.
- Works with preceding required params and default params.
- Added tests: `TestVariadicFunctions` in eval_test.go (9 cases including zero
  args, single arg, multiple args, with required params, with defaults).
